  "question": {
    "text": "The excess pressure inside a soap bubble is thrice the excess pressure inside a second soap bubble. The ratio between the volume of the first and the second bubble is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$1: 9$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$1: 3$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$1: 27$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$1: 81$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0034_99e62c26e89d.png\"/>\n$\\mathrm{P}_1-\\mathrm{P}_0=\\frac{4 \\mathrm{~T}}{\\mathrm{r}_1}  \\qquad \\quad \\quad \\quad\\mathrm{P}_2-\\mathrm{P}_0=\\frac{4 \\mathrm{~T}}{\\mathrm{r}_2}$\n$\\begin{aligned} &amp; \\mathrm{P}_1-\\mathrm{P}_0=3\\left(\\mathrm{P}_2-\\mathrm{P}_0\\right) \\\\ &amp; \\frac{4 \\mathrm{~T}}{\\mathrm{r}_1}=3 \\frac{4 \\mathrm{~T}}{\\mathrm{r}_2} \\\\ &amp; \\mathrm{r}_2=3 \\mathrm{r}_1 \\\\ &amp; \\frac{\\mathrm{V}_1}{\\mathrm{~V}_2}=\\frac{\\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\mathrm{r}_1^3}{\\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\mathrm{r}_2^3}=\\frac{1}{27}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
